fork: write G-code preview thumbnails from the CLI

The headless CLI (--slice) passed a null thumbnail callback to
Print::export_gcode, so the printer's thumbnails setting (e.g.
96x96/PNG, 300x300/PNG) was ignored and printer UIs (Mainsail, Fluidd,
Moonraker) showed no preview for CLI-sliced files.

Factor the CLI's offscreen renderer (hidden GLFW window, OpenGLManager,
thumbnail shader, model volumes) out of the 3MF export block into
CliThumbnailRenderer, set up lazily on first use, and use it both as the
G-code thumbnail callback and for the 3MF plate images. Without OpenGL
the failure is logged once and the G-code is written without
thumbnails; the exit code is unchanged. GLFW is told not to switch the
working directory to the app bundle's Resources on macOS, so relative
output paths still resolve after the first render.

